        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/432915?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">This PR adds a guide to federated identity.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">It's not finished yet, but it's definitely ready for some review.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">What's done</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>an overview of what it is</li>\n<li>a moderately close look at the main flow in OpenID Connect</li>\n<li>a short but sufficient (I think) discussion of the use of third-party cookies in federated identity systems</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">What's not done:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>a section on using specific identity providers. I want to say, people adding support for federated identity will always need to choose a provider, and providers will greatly reduce the amount of complexity they need to deal with. I think it is most helpful to name specific providers, such as Google and GitHub and (in a slightly different way I suppose) Auth0 but I don't like the idea of seeming to pick winners or entrench monopolies.</li>\n<li>a section introducing FedCM. I want especially to talk about:\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>how this fixes third-party cookie issues, greatly simplifies the work the RP needs to do, and promises a better and more consistent UX</li>\n<li>how it's not cross-browser yet (and thus can't really be recommended yet) but that we're hopeful it will become so.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>probably something tying it together, which should describe some of the limitations of fed ID (especially, about it excluding people who don't want to or can't sign up with your chosen IdP).</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><strong>Note that preview images are broken because of <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3510366053\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/fred/issues/904\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/fred/issues/904/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/fred/issues/904\">mdn/fred#904</a>.</strong></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41779",
            "title": "Add a federated identity guide",
            "date_modified": "2025-11-03T00:29:10.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-11-02T19:29:56.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "wbamberg",
                "url": "https://github.com/wbamberg"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/160616048?u=c67d934d3d5438fa90d22a59e3c49636cd31c75c&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">What</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Clarify that <code class=\"notranslate\">X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff</code> also affects document navigations:<br>\nuser agents should avoid sniffing and treating content as HTML when the <code class=\"notranslate\">Content-Type</code> is incorrect or missing.</li>\n<li>Add a short subsection “Effect on HTML document sniffing” with references.</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Why</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>The current page focuses on scripts and styles; this update reflects the MIME sniffing algorithm behavior for documents as discussed in WHATWG.</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">How to verify</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Run <code class=\"notranslate\">yarn start</code> and preview /en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/X-Content-Type-Options.</li>\n<li>Confirm the new subsection is rendered and links work.</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">References</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>WHATWG MIME Sniffing algorithm: <a href=\"https://mimesniff.spec.whatwg.org/#mime-type-sniffing-algorithm\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://mimesniff.spec.whatwg.org/#mime-type-sniffing-algorithm</a></li>\n<li>Discussion: <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"424897683\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/whatwg/mimesniff/issues/98\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/whatwg/mimesniff/issues/98/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/whatwg/mimesniff/issues/98\">whatwg/mimesniff#98</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #41745.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3570561352\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41745\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/41745/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41745\">#41745</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41776",
            "title": "docs(HTTP): X-Content-Type-Options — mention impact on document sniffing",
            "date_modified": "2025-11-03T15:46:14.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-11-02T13:31:42.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "ssswdwads",
                "url": "https://github.com/ssswdwads"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55398995?u=9f6a9837c9879eceb0abde487a338b92d4e206fc&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">Our style guide requires JS identifiers to use camelCase. Some of these make sense as snake_case, but it is more important to be consistent than to make sense from a stylistic perspective.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41775",
            "title": "Lint: camelCase JavaScript identifiers",
            "date_modified": "2025-11-03T09:52:00.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-11-02T04:59:32.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "Josh-Cena",
                "url": "https://github.com/Josh-Cena"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55398995?u=9f6a9837c9879eceb0abde487a338b92d4e206fc&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">HTML <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;tbody&gt;</code> elements can have both start/end tags omitted, but it's still present in the DOM, which can be extremely unintuitive for selectors/DOM operations. Instead of relying on this implicit behavior, it's better to make the <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;tbody&gt;</code> explicit where possible.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR should be very easy to review with hide whitespace turned on.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41774",
            "title": "Lint: HTML tables should have explicit <tbody> tag",
            "date_modified": "2025-11-03T09:46:32.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-11-02T04:26:44.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "Josh-Cena",
                "url": "https://github.com/Josh-Cena"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55398995?u=9f6a9837c9879eceb0abde487a338b92d4e206fc&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">Follow up of <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3572980693\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41754\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/41754/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41754\">#41754</a>.</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Tag <code class=\"notranslate\">vue</code> code blocks properly</li>\n<li>Remove illicit <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;iframe&gt;</code> children; I know this is for fallback but there's no reason to care about lack of <code class=\"notranslate\">iframe</code> support</li>\n<li>Buttons and links should have accessible names</li>\n<li>Images should have <code class=\"notranslate\">src</code></li>\n<li>Fix invalid nesting, such as <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;menu&gt;</code> having non-<code class=\"notranslate\">li</code> children</li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;map&gt;</code> need a name, and if it has an id they need to be equal. Also slightly updated the docs for <code class=\"notranslate\">HTMLImageElement.useMap</code> to reflect this</li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">id</code> should be valid CSS identifiers</li>\n<li>Fix a case where we do <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;legend role=\"button\"&gt;</code> to use an actual button instead</li>\n<li>Properly escape <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">&gt;</code>; properly add trailing slashes for void elements</li>\n<li>Boolean attributes have no value</li>\n<li>Remove deprecated attributes</li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">street-address</code> is not a valid <code class=\"notranslate\">autocomplete</code> token for <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;input&gt;</code>; replaced with <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;textarea&gt;</code></li>\n<li>Labels cannot label multiple controls: there are a few cases where we use the pattern <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;label for=\"a\"&gt;&lt;output&gt;&lt;/output&gt;&lt;/label&gt;&lt;input id=\"a\"&gt;</code> where we don't actually intend for the <code class=\"notranslate\">output</code> to be a form control, so replaced it with <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;span&gt;</code> instead</li>\n</ul>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41771",
            "title": "Lint: HTML conformance/style fixes (2)",
            "date_modified": "2025-11-03T15:41:28.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-11-01T06:56:55.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "Josh-Cena",
